      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the FDA-labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of serious GI effects and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nCould this be a typo? These are some common regimens:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg twice daily**, or 500 mg three times daily, if you're starting or titrating\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
